The error `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'city')` means `order.shipping_address` is `undefined` at runtime. When you try to read `.city` on `undefined`, JavaScript throws a `TypeError`.

## Why it works locally but not in production

Your local/test data always has `shipping_address` fully populated. In production, some orders arrive without a `shipping_address` (e.g., digital goods, incomplete checkouts, or a different API schema). The nested property access crashes instead of gracefully degrading.

## Fix

Use optional chaining (`?.`) to safely traverse the nested path. If any link in the chain is `undefined`/`null`, the expression short-circuits to `undefined` instead of throwing — and the `|| "standard"` fallback handles the rest.

